Call $T$:
- irreducible if there is no proper closed subspace $Y\subsetneq X$ with $T_a(Y)\subseteq Y$ for all $a\in A$;
- $n$-fold irreducible if for every $n$-tuple $(x_1,\dots,x_n)$ of linearly independent vectors in $X$, the orbit $\{(T_a x_1,\dots,T_a x_n) : a\in A\}$ is dense in $X^n$ (in the product topology);
- totally irreducible if $T$ is $n$-fold irreducible for every positive integer $n$.

The commutant of $T$ is $\{S\in L(X) : ST_a = T_a S \text{ for all } a\in A\}$.

Question: If $T$ is irreducible and its commutant consists only of scalar multiples of the identity operator on $X$, must $T$ be totally irreducible?","macro_subject":"Analysis","category_tag":"Representations on locally convex spaces","open_status":"partially_solved","status_search_result":"The question, posed by Fell and Doran, is known to be open in full generality for representations on arbitrary complex locally convex spaces. Partial affirmative results are known: for instance, Żelazko (Studia Mathematica, 1998) proved that on the F-space (s) and more generally on infinite topological products of the scalar field, every irreducible representation with trivial (scalar) commutant is totally irreducible. No general resolution for arbitrary locally convex X appears in the literature.","status_evidence":[{"title":"A density theorem for algebra representations on the space (s)","url":"https://eudml.org/doc/216559","snippet":"An arbitrary irreducible representation of a real or complex algebra on the F-space (s), or more generally on an arbitrary infinite topological product of the field of scalars, is totally irreducible provided its commutant is trivial, which provides an affirmative solution to a problem of Fell and Doran for representations on these spaces.","claim":"Affirmative answer is known in the special case of representations on (s) and on infinite products of the scalar field; the question is attributed to Fell and Doran."}],"confidence":0.75},"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"aa80b3bc-53f2-471e-970c-1c0ca4d48dd2"}
